### Quick Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] All core flows (search → add to cart → checkout) tested.  
- [ ] Responsive design passes on mobile, tablet, desktop.  
- [ ] Accessibility score ≥ 90% (WCAG 2.1 AA).  
- [ ] SEO meta tags present on all pages.  
- [ ] Error boundaries in place.  
- [ ] Analytics & error monitoring configured.  
- [ ] Backup strategy for product data.  

---

## 🎉 Final Thought

Building a front‑end for an e‑commerce site is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small—get a minimal viable product (MVP) up and running, then iterate based on real user data. Keep the code modular, test often, and let the community’s best practices guide you. Happy coding! 🚀

If you’d like help with a specific part (e.g., setting up Stripe, optimizing images, or writing tests), just let me know!
